---RAM* program---
PC=03
 1: +000 -                                                                    
 2: +000 -                                                                    
 3: +004   (= PC starting setting: 03)          FAST BOOTSTRAP PROGRAM:       
 4: +000         <------                        For loading instructions      
 5: +204   CLA         |                        from  Input  into memory.     
 6: +400   ADD 1       |                                                      
 7: +304   STO         |                                                      
 8: +704          ------                      INPUT  format example:          
 9: +000                                        010   = First memory address  
10: +000                                        030    --                     
11: +000                                        031     |                     
12: +000                                        230     |                     
13: +000                                        431     |  =  ADD.RAM program 
14: +000                                        332     |                     
15: +000                                        132     |                     
16: +000                                        910    --                     
17: +000                                        [blank]                       
18: +000 -                                                                    
19: +000 -                                                                    
20: +000 -                                                                    
21: +000                RAM* also has a "hardwired" SLOW BOOTSTRAP:           
22: +000                just the "001" in memory cell 00 (due to              
23: +000                David Hagelbarger, Bell Laboratories).                
24: +000 -                                                                    
25: +000                Slow bootstrap  INPUT  format example:                
26: +000                  002  -For Slow                                      
27: +000                  700  - Boot.                                        
28: +000                  010  -memory address, for                           
29: +000                  030  -program instruction.                          
30: +000                  011  -address                                       
31: +000                  031  -instruction                                   
32: +000                  012  -address                                       
33: +000                  230  -instruction                                   
34: +000                  013  -address                  =  ADD.RAM program   
35: +000                  431  -instruction                                   
36: +000                  014  -address                                       
37: +000                  332  -instruction                                   
38: +000                  015  -address                                       
39: +000                  132  -instruction                                   
40: +000                  016  -address                                       
41: +000                  910  -instruction                                   
42: +000                  [blank]                                             
43: +000 -                                                                    
44: +000                PC must start at memory cell  00  for Slow Boot.      
45: +000 -                                                                    
46: +000 -                                                                    
47: +000 -                                                                    
48: +000                Slow Boot can be used to load Fast Boot,              
49: +000                and Fast Boot in turn used to load, e.g.,             
50: +000                ADD.RAM .                                             
